<section id="A1.SS3.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.3.2 </span>Text Corpus</h4>

<div id="A1.SS3.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We use script-appropriate text for each writing system. Latin samples consist of pangrams, common phrases, and typographic test sentences in English (e.g., “The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog”). Chinese samples consist of common phrases in Simplified Chinese selected for glyph coverage across the two available fonts. Arabic and Devanagari samples use representative phrases chosen for natural appearance and good glyph coverage.</p>
</div>
</section>
