</section>
<section id="A3.SS2.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">C.2.2 </span>Statistical Significance</h4>

<div id="A3.SS2.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Using McNemar’s test for pairwise model comparisons: Gemini-3-Flash is significantly better than all other models (<math id="A3.SS2.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&lt;0.001" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.001</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&lt;0.001</annotation></semantics></math>). GPT-5.2 and Claude-Sonnet-4.6 are significantly better than middle-tier models (<math id="A3.SS2.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&lt;0.05" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.05</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&lt;0.05</annotation></semantics></math>). Pairwise differences among the middle-tier cluster (Qwen3-VL-30B-A3B, Doubao-Seed-1.6, Qwen3-Max, Gemini-3-Pro, Qwen3-VL-32B, Qwen2.5-VL-7B, Qwen2.5-VL-72B, Qwen3-VL-8B) are not statistically significant (<math id="A3.SS2.SSS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&gt;0.05" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0.05</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&gt;0.05</annotation></semantics></math>), consistent with their overlapping confidence intervals. GLM-4.5V and Pixtral-12B are not significantly different from the 25% random baseline (<math id="A3.SS2.SSS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&gt;0.05" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0.05</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&gt;0.05</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.3 </span>Perception Hierarchy Illustration</h3>

<div id="A3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#A3.F8" title="Figure 8 ‣ C.3 Perception Hierarchy Illustration ‣ Appendix C Complete Results and Statistical Analysis" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> visualizes the perception hierarchy discussed in §<a href="#S4.SS2" title="4.2 The Perception Hierarchy ‣ 4 Diagnostic Evaluation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a> of the main paper. The four typographic properties are arranged by their computational complexity within ViT-based encoders, from zeroth-order pixel statistics for color to second-order relational comparisons for style.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.F8" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2603.08497v1/figs/hierarchy_concept.png" id="A3.F8.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:405/214;" width="405" height="214" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A3.F8.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 8</span>: </span><span id="A3.F8.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Perception hierarchy.<span id="A3.F8.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Typographic properties map onto increasing visual feature complexity: color (0th-order pixel statistics, 89–100%) <math id="A3.F8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gg" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≫</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gg</annotation></semantics></math> family (1st-order glyph shape, 26–81%) <math id="A3.F8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&gt;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>&gt;</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&gt;</annotation></semantics></math> size (1st-order spatial extent, 22–52%) <math id="A3.F8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&gt;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>&gt;</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&gt;</annotation></semantics></math> style (2nd-order relational comparison, 23–34%). Dashed line marks the 25% random-chance baseline.</span></span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.4 </span>Accuracy Heatmap</h3>

<div id="A3.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#A3.F9" title="Figure 9 ‣ C.4 Accuracy Heatmap ‣ Appendix C Complete Results and Statistical Analysis" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> presents a per-model, per-property accuracy heatmap that provides a comprehensive view of the results in Table 2 of the main paper. Models are sorted by overall accuracy from top to bottom.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.F9" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2603.08497v1/heatmap.png" id="A3.F9.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:357/388;" width="357" height="388" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A3.F9.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 9</span>: </span><span id="A3.F9.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Model <math id="A3.F9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math> property accuracy heatmap. A clear perception hierarchy emerges: color is trivially solved, while style remains universally poor. Gemini-3-Flash leads across all properties; GLM-4.5V performs at near-random levels.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Fine-Tuning Details</h2>

<section id="A4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.1 </span>LoRA Configuration</h3>

<div id="A4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<div id="A4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_listing ltx_lst_language_Python ltx_lstlisting ltx_listing"><div class="ltx_listing_data"><a href="data:text/plain;base64," download="">⬇</a></div>
<div id="lstnumberx1" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;">lora_config</span><span id="lstnumberx1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;">=</span><span id="lstnumberx1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;">{</span>
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx2" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;">    </span><span id="lstnumberx2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_string ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;">"r"</span><span id="lstnumberx2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;">:</span><span id="lstnumberx2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;">16,</span>
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx3" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;">    </span><span id="lstnumberx3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_string ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;">"lora_alpha"</span><span id="lstnumberx3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;">:</span><span id="lstnumberx3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx3.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;">32,</span>
</div>
